fix(podman_info): detect rootful bridge instead of defaulting to pasta

Rootful engines report rootlessNetworkCmd even though it is unused,
and host.security.rootless=false was ignored. network_mode therefore
fell through to "pasta", so _upstream_dns_for_mode returned PASTA_DNS
(169.254.1.1) — unreachable from a bridge netns, leaving dnsmasq
unable to forward and containers unable to resolve any name.

- PodmanInfo gains rootless (default True for backward compatibility)
- network_mode returns "bridge" when rootful
- _upstream_dns_for_mode("bridge") reads the host's /etc/resolv.conf
- _gateways_for_mode("bridge") returns ("", "")
- drop the `or "pasta"` fallback that masked the misclassification

Repro: rootful podman machine, terok-shield run <ctr> -- alpine wget https://pypi.org
Before: wget: bad address 'pypi.org'. After: resolves.